      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-243109",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/a2/a2da9c128b9fa38695760dd0e7ecd0c5c4ca9778eeb8f7cb770396982e420d9c.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, $EFGH$ is a parallelogram, and $m\u2220G = 90^{\u2218}$.\n\nConsider the following statement:\n\n> *$EFGH$ is a rectangle.*\n\nThe table below gives the proof of the statement. Select the correct options in the table and thus complete the proof.\n\n|  | Statement | Reason |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| 1 | $EFGH$ is a parallelogram | {{field-1}} |\n| 2 | $m\u2220G = 90^{\u2218}$ | {{field-2}} |\n| 3 | $\u2220H$ and $\u2220G$ are supplementary | {{field-3}} |\n| 4 | $m\u2220H + m\u2220G = 180^{\u2218}$ | {{field-4}} |\n| 5 | $m\u2220H + 90^{\u2218} = 180^{\u2218}$ | {{field-5}} |\n| 6 | $m\u2220H = 90^{\u2218}$ | {{field-6}} |\n| 7 | $\u2220H$ and $\u2220G$ are right angles | {{field-7}} |\n| 8 | $\u2220H\u2245\u2220F$ and $\u2220G\u2245\u2220E$ | {{field-8}} |\n| 9 | $\u2220E$ and $\u2220F$ are right angles | {{field-9}} |\n| 10 | $EFGH$ is a rectangle | {{field-10}} |"
    },
